t.pdf
mtest.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Threshold-fit run tree (omni_thr_fit/) -- what is deliberately NOT committed.
#
# The rule: commit anything expensive to REGENERATE, exclude anything large that
# a re-run reproduces. The banked predictions (online_pred.jsonl, ~6.6 MB) ARE
# committed -- they are ~150 GPU-hours of results and the whole study is
# re-scorable from them offline. The per-tick run logs are not: 444 MB that any
# re-run reproduces and nothing downstream reads except the AUC audit.
#
# NOTE: git treats "#" as a comment ONLY at the start of a line. An inline
# comment after a pattern becomes part of the pattern and silently matches
# nothing -- which is exactly what happened on the first draft of this block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# a full copy of this same repo, made so a run never mutates the source tree.
# Recreate it by copying this checkout; do not version it twice (2.4 GB).
omni_thr_fit/repo/

# verbose per-tick logs, 444 MB across 556 files, fully regenerable
omni_thr_fit/**/run.log

# torch core dumps (7 GB apparent size, sparse on disk)
core_*

# local before/after backups of edited scripts
*.bak_*

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Never commit credentials. .env is ignored above too; this is a second barrier
# because the keys in it are live and do NOT match the usual AIza.../sk-...
# shapes a secret scanner looks for.
.env
*.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ...but the fit tree's own logs ARE the profiling record, so un-ignore them.
#
# The blanket "*.log" above is inherited from the system tree, where logs are
# throwaway. In omni_thr_fit/logs/ they are not: lane_*.log carries per-unit
# timings, xRT and model-load costs, and thrfit_*.log is the SLURM record of
# which generation did what. 10.8 MB across 90 files, and no re-run reproduces
# them, because they describe one specific run on specific hardware.
#
# This does NOT re-admit results/**/run.log (444 MB of per-tick output): that
# lives under results/, not logs/, and stays excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!omni_thr_fit/logs/*.log
!omni_thr_fit/logs/*.err
!omni_thr_fit/logs/*.out
